1) What is IDE?
A) An IDE stands for Integrated Development Environment where all the tools required for a developer
is put in one place like the place to write code, to run code and to navigate between files. It also gives
some cool features like integration to git, auto suggestions, syntax highlighting.

2) How to run a python program without IDE?
A) Open the terminal where the file is present and enter the command
> python3 filename.py

3) What is the difference between code editor and IDE?
A) Code editor means just to write the code provides syntax highlighting for example notepad,
but IDE gives tools for development and testing like run, debug ,git which helps to make life of developers easy.